 qualify:["DTI is usually calculated on a qualifying payment (often fully amortizing or interest-only at a stressed rate) - lender-specific","Full-doc income is standard; some lenders now offer bank-statement or non-QM HELOCs (typical, lender-specific)","Valuation can be AVM, desktop, drive-by or full appraisal depending on line size and CLTV","Title must show the first lien and any other liens; existing subordinate liens usually must be paid off or subordinated"],
 docs:["Current first mortgage statement","Recent pay stubs and W-2s or tax returns","Homeowners insurance declarations page","Property tax bill and HOA statement if applicable","Government ID","Payoff letters for any debts being consolidated"],
